Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.820 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  multiplayer online battle arena games or  MOBAs have gained immense popularity in  the last few years with games dota 2 and  League of Legends hitting over 8 million  and 64 million monthly active players  respectively not to mention the millions  of dollars being awarded in the  competitive scene if you're unfamiliar  with the genre members usually play from  a top-down perspective you and a small  team of friends each control a single  character with unique abilities and  attempt to push into the enemy base and  destroyers the large followings of dota  2 and League of Legends have inspired  several triple-a developers to come out  with their own interpretations of the  MOBA formula let's see what some of the  big names have to offer  developed by waystone games and  published by EA dawn gauge says a lot of  gameplay similarities to dota 2 and  League of Legends  however dawn Gate firsts what the  developers call a flexible metal what  does that even mean well in dota 2 and  League of Legends the character you  choose to play pretty much defines your  role in the match a particular  character's abilities might naturally  make them much more suitable to act as a  healing support rather than a damaged  soaking tank for example so the variety  of character combinations that can make  up a team's roster is a huge part of  what is called the meta game but in  Dorne gates players have the option to  pick their role no matter what character  they're playing this is because  selecting different roles affects the  attributes and perks that your character  gets you might earn more currency each  time you kill an enemy player or get a  helpless when you kill neutral creatures  the one gate gives you the tools to play  the same character in vastly different  ways and this flexible meta is its main  draw card  Crytek arena of fate is going for  something punchy R and more accessible  by limiting its matches to 20 minutes  the game still features a large pool of  characters to choose from and the  objective of destroying the enemy teams  base however if the 20 minutes is up and  birth bases still stand  then the team with the most points is  the winner attribute boosting abilities  are unlocked as you level an alternative  to buying attribute boosting items in  shop areas like in dota 2 or League of  Legends making matches faster paced and  getting rid of the need to remember  recipe combination  in Dead Island epidemic items take on a  more persistent role brought to you by  the same people who published at Island  the game calls itself the world's first  zombie mobile or Zomba Dead Island  epidemic features a crafting system that  has players collecting blueprints and  item parts during matches to make and  upgrade their own weapons to use in the  future gameplay revolves around  surviving waves of zombies in addition  to fighting other humans you can also  choose just to fight NPC zombies the  game differentiates itself by letting up  to three different teams of players  battle it out and relies on WASD key  inputs for movement and the mouse to aim  as you can imagine Dead Island epidemic  is a lot more action orientated and  could be mistaken for a top-down shooter  Wizards heroes of the storm draws its  content from the universes of its  existing catalogue of games  this means a roster of characters from  the starcraft Warcraft and Diablo series  like in arena of fate Blizzard is aiming  for matches around 20 minutes long  although this isn't a hard limit the  timeliness is encouraged through the  game's leveling system which has whole  teams leveling up together similar to  arena of fate heroes of the storm has no  items or shops to worry about which gets  rid of the need to consider that extra  information maps specific objectives  regularly popping up encourages the two  teams to confront each other more often  to be completely honest with you it's  hard to imagine MOBA players like myself  breaking away from the games we've  already diverted so much time - but on  the other hand the flexibility themes  and shorter learning curves being  offered by games like dawn Gate arena  fate Dead Island epidemic and heroes of  the storm could bring in a lot of new  players to the genre and give veterans  different things to get excited about do  any of the mentioned games offer  something that interests you or have you  got your heart already set on a  particular game if you've never played a  MOBA game before  what would it have to have to interest  you let us know in the comments below

